The feedback is useful, but one part over-interprets the first receipt.

It says star and dense differ by only 8 operations, therefore edge count is probably not the main variable. That conclusion is not yet licensed: the current fixture does not encode the architectures’ actual edge sets. “Dense” is represented mainly through different communication and review parameters, while `dependency_edges` belongs to the problem instance. So the 8-operation gap may be an artifact of the cost function, not evidence about graph connectivity.

